{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Standing [G/B]by your window in [C]pain,
[G]a [G/B]pistol in your [C]hand
[G]and i [G/B]beg you, dear [C]molly, girl,
[D]Try and understand your man the best you can.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Across the great [A7]divide
just [C]grab your hat, and [Em]take that [G]ride
[G]Get yourself a [A7]bride
and [C]bring your children [Em]down to the river [G]side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I had a goal in my [C]younger days,
[G]I nearly wrote my [C]will
[G]But I changed my [C]mind for the better,
[D]I'm at the still, had my fill and I'm fit to kill
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Pinball machine, and a queen,
I nearly took a bust
Tried to keep my hands to myself,
ya say it's a must, but who can ya trust?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Harvest moon shining down from the sky,
a weary sign for all
I'm gonna leave this one horse town,
had to stall till the fall, now I'm gonna crawl
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Across the great divide
Instrumental for the rest of the verse
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Now molly dear, don't ya shed a tear
Your time will surely come,
you'll feed your man chicken every Sunday
Now tell me, hon, whatcha done with the gun?
{end_of_verse}
